experiment: slotwin
  the question      §58. §53 read the derived index's slot term as a null
                    POOLED OVER THE WHOLE SESSION. §56 then showed that
                    index is degenerate in 22 and 18 of 24 creatures in the
                    first two eighths and 16 of 24 in the last, and PERFECT
                    in all 24 through e4-e7. Does it express THERE?
  the contradiction §54 left AVERAGING standing: (1-2w) of ceiling. At the
                    derived arm's measured w = 0.1712 that is +0.0850, and §53
                    measured +0.0081 +- 0.0170 -- short by 4.53 SE. Already in
                    the archive, never stated.
  the method        §53's EXACT primary -- the SLOT TERM, where (n_0s - n_1s)
                    IS the label difference, so it is a DEPENDENCE and not a
                    magnitude -- scored over a PRE-REGISTERED window. One
                    per-probe vector added; no core change, no RNG draw.
  the two models    §53's NULL: 0.    AVERAGING in CLEAN (w 0.0326): +0.1209,
                    which is 93.5% of the pinned ceiling +0.1293.
  session           900.0 s of simulated life x 120 sessions, 4 arms
  instrument        slotwin   trial seed 0000000001357f69   120 sessions
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

  THE PREDICTION'S ARITHMETIC SELF-CHECK, which is not a result. (1-2w) is
  LINEAR in w, so the probe-weighted mean of the per-phase predictions must
  equal the prediction at the session-mean rate. If these disagree one of
  the two arithmetics is wrong and nothing below should be read.
    per-phase, weighted 2:1:4:1   +0.086172
    at the session-mean w 0.1668    +0.086172
    identity                      +0.00e+00   PASS

  CLAUSE 4's SIX BRANCHES, exercised on synthetic input before any real
  row reaches them. E = 0.0241 (the projected CLEAN SE), A = +0.1209.
    S -0.0600  A +0.1209  -> ARTEFACT DOMINATES                 ok  (below -2E)
    S +0.0100  A +0.1209  -> §53's NULL SURVIVES               ok  (inside +-2E)
    S +0.0600  A +0.1209  -> PARTIAL                            ok  (above 2E, below A-2E)
    S +0.1209  A +0.1209  -> EXPRESSES AS AVERAGING PREDICTS    ok  (within 2E of A)
    S +0.2000  A +0.1209  -> OVER-EXPRESSES                     ok  (above A+2E)
    S +0.0600  A +0.0723  -> UNDEFINED -- the models are closer than 4 SE ok  (A < 4E: the gate must REFUSE, not pick)
    branches reachable  6/6  PASS

  CLAUSE 0 (FIRST) -- IDENTITY. The windowed scorer run over ALL probes
  must reproduce `cell_g`/`cell_n`, and through them §53's PUBLISHED table.
  If this fails the windowed numbers are not §53's session and NOTHING
  below is readable. The archive half is budget-bound and says so.
    reconstruction, worst over all 120 creatures   0.00e+00   PASS
    T1.RET       pooled SLOT +0.0081 +- 0.0170   §53 +0.0081 +- 0.0170   match
    T1.RET.D     pooled SLOT -0.0947 +- 0.0306   §53 -0.0947 +- 0.0306   match
    T1.ORACLE.D  pooled SLOT +0.0211 +- 0.0327   §53 +0.0211 +- 0.0327   match
    T1.ORACLE    pooled SLOT +0.1293 +- 0.0478   §53 +0.1293 +- 0.0478   match

  CLAUSE 1 -- BOOKKEEPING, PER EIGHTH. A pinned index makes the cells
  DIAGONAL, so T1.ORACLE's residual is identically zero and its slot term
  IS its gap. Arithmetic, not a result -- and a windowed scorer has to earn
  it again in every eighth. `ident` is gap - (slot + residual), worst case.
    ORACLE residual, worst eighth        0.00e+00   over 81 creature-eighths   PASS
    identity, worst creature x eighth    1.11e-16   PASS
    and over EVERY arm and eighth        1.67e-16   over 807 creature-eighths   PASS

  CLAUSE 2 -- VACUITY, at the PRIMARY'S GRANULARITY and on the arm that is
  KNOWN to express. The question a vacuity gate must answer here is whether
  a ~17-probe window can carry a large slot term AT ALL, and only an arm
  that expresses can answer it -- the derived arm's own column could not
  (`vacuity-gate-cannot-guard-a-rejection`).

  THE THRESHOLD IS THE ARM'S OWN POOLED VALUE AND NOT A CONSTANT, and the
  450k smoke is why: an absolute 0.08 was calibrated on §53's 900k ceiling
  and read 3/8 at 450k, where the arm's OWN pooled figure is only +0.0827.
  That gate could have failed with nothing wrong (`baseprobe-gate`).
  Required: the per-eighth MEAN recovers at least half of what the pooled
  estimator sees on the same arm at the same budget, and >= 6 of 8 eighths
  are strictly positive.
    T1.ORACLE  slot +0.1299 +0.1260 -0.0171 +0.0678 +0.1238 +0.1665 +0.1747 -0.1654 
               n         12      12      12      11      11      11      11       1 
    per-eighth mean +0.0758  vs half the pooled +0.0646 (pooled +0.1293)   PASS
    eighths strictly positive   6/8   PASS

  CLAUSE 3 -- TRANSFER. The phase cut comes from §56's `slotdrift` DERIVED
  arm, which runs pin_mode 5: a DIFFERENT enclosing experiment, so transfer
  is TESTED and not assumed. §56's modal rule over §56's cut, on §58's own
